00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.957
<i>Let me tell you a story about a young man called Oliver.</i>


00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:46.374
<i>There's no singing. No dancing.
And definitely no happy ending.</i>


00:00:47.205 --> 00:00:49.062
<i>But before we get to me,</i>


00:00:49.095 --> 00:00:51.399
<i>this all started with a thief
called Tom Chitling.</i>


00:01:00.134 --> 00:01:01.254
There he is!


00:01:01.287 --> 00:01:02.823
Stop! Stop!


00:01:21.031 --> 00:01:22.696
Let's go!


00:01:52.581 --> 00:01:54.919
- Come here! Where is it?
- I don't have it.


00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.383
<i>Growing up,
it was just me and Mum.</i>


00:02:41.414 --> 00:02:44.838
<i>We didn't have a lot,
but we had our imagination.</i>


00:02:45.638 --> 00:02:47.655
Where'd you take us
today, Oliver?


00:02:47.686 --> 00:02:50.566
The beach.
And we had an ice cream.


00:02:50.597 --> 00:02:52.359
Mmm, delicious.


00:02:53.318 --> 00:02:56.261
I took us
to the circus.


00:02:56.294 --> 00:02:58.951
Wow. Elephants.


00:02:58.982 --> 00:03:00.775
- Thanks, Mum.
- You're welcome.


00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:03.143
I'm gonna take us somewhere
even better tomorrow.


00:03:05.926 --> 00:03:07.527
I can't wait.


00:03:11.174 --> 00:03:12.807
What do you see?


00:03:12.837 --> 00:03:14.470
A lady swimming.


00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.358
What else?


00:03:17.255 --> 00:03:19.335
What does Oliver see?


00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.222
I don't understand,
Mum.


00:03:21.253 --> 00:03:25.798
Well, I see escape.


00:03:27.047 --> 00:03:29.703
I see a powerful woman


00:03:29.735 --> 00:03:31.783
leaving behind a life
that wasn't meant for her.


00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:36.551
And all of the flowers,
they're telling us why.


00:03:38.598 --> 00:03:42.214
Anyone ever told you
you're a bit weird, Mum?


00:03:42.886 --> 00:03:46.951
Has anyone ever told you
you're a bit cheeky?


00:03:46.981 --> 00:03:48.647
Shh!


00:03:48.679 --> 00:03:52.775
Oh. We're going
to space now, are we?


00:03:52.805 --> 00:03:53.862
Yeah.


00:03:55.078 --> 00:03:58.279
I thought we were supposed to be
doing our dreams for the future.


00:03:59.847 --> 00:04:01.511
I don't get it.


00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:04.358
Well that's you.
And that's me.


00:04:04.391 --> 00:04:06.311
And we're
in a gallery.


00:04:06.341 --> 00:04:10.022
And we're looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery


00:04:10.055 --> 00:04:12.102
looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery.


00:04:12.134 --> 00:04:14.119
And it goes on
and on and on...


00:04:14.919 --> 00:04:16.934
<i>But nothing
lasts forever.</i>


00:04:23.461 --> 00:04:25.189
<i>Then it was just me.</i>


00:04:25.222 --> 00:04:26.918
Poor lad.


00:04:28.966 --> 00:04:30.438
Time to go, Oliver.


00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.134
<i>I didn't know
anyone else.</i>


00:04:33.957 --> 00:04:35.814
<i>I certainly didn't belong
with them.</i>


00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.023
<i>I was better off on my own.</i>


00:04:52.006 --> 00:04:53.959
Oi! Wake up.


00:04:55.302 --> 00:04:57.126
Wake up,
you little rat.


00:04:57.158 --> 00:04:59.302
Right. I've told you before,
and I'm not... Hey!


00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:00.743
I'm not gonna
tell you again!


00:05:01.317 --> 00:05:02.823
Don't you dare.


00:05:02.855 --> 00:05:04.614
Sod off,
you little scrounger!


00:05:04.646 --> 00:05:07.047
Stop sleeping
in the gallery!


00:05:07.078 --> 00:05:09.702
<i>People don't really call
me Oliver any more. They call me...</i>


00:07:04.102 --> 00:07:07.270
Congratulations, love.


00:07:07.302 --> 00:07:08.710
You've won
a little yellow square.


00:07:08.741 --> 00:07:10.405
You could see
I had my hands full.


00:07:10.438 --> 00:07:11.814
They're not my rules.
I just enforce 'em.


00:07:11.846 --> 00:07:13.222
I was right here.


00:07:13.254 --> 00:07:14.566
You was right here
for too long.


00:07:14.598 --> 00:07:16.263
I thought
you were gonna move in.


00:07:16.294 --> 00:07:18.118
Do you think
I like doing this?


00:07:18.149 --> 00:07:20.486
Actually, I do.
It makes me feel big in every way.


00:07:20.518 --> 00:07:22.311
Could you not give
the ticket to anyone else?


00:07:22.342 --> 00:07:24.070
I'm not just giving 'em
to nice people.


00:07:24.101 --> 00:07:25.702
You look like a nice person,
so I've given one to you.


00:07:25.733 --> 00:07:27.558
Please, I was literally
about to leave.


00:07:27.589 --> 00:07:28.934
You should have left earlier,
shouldn't you?


00:07:28.965 --> 00:07:30.630
I can't afford this ticket.


00:07:30.662 --> 00:07:32.679
Well, I can't afford a 4K TV,
but I wish I could.


00:07:32.709 --> 00:07:34.278
I'd like one of those.


00:07:34.309 --> 00:07:36.166
Actually, I don't even know
what it is,


00:07:36.198 --> 00:07:38.278
but I like the sound of owning it.
I wish I could have it.


00:07:38.309 --> 00:07:40.133
- Please, sir...
- Please, please, please.


00:07:40.165 --> 00:07:41.894
Don't tell me
your problems.


00:07:41.925 --> 00:07:43.813
You're gonna get another one
in a minute. Oi!


00:07:43.845 --> 00:07:46.598
Hey, stay away from that van.
That's my van, you little pig.


00:07:57.254 --> 00:07:59.079
- Here you go, miss.
- Thank you.


00:08:07.109 --> 00:08:08.486
Stop that lad!


00:08:26.309 --> 00:08:28.454
Yo, man. The bikes!


00:08:41.797 --> 00:08:43.397
Yo, likkle man!


00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.182
Yo!


00:08:46.885 --> 00:08:48.775
- Hey, slow up, bro.
- What?


00:08:49.671 --> 00:08:53.094
Relax, man.
The cops packed it in way back.


00:08:53.125 --> 00:08:54.471
Why are you chasing me then?


00:08:54.502 --> 00:08:56.230
'Cause you forgot
your shopping.


00:08:59.013 --> 00:09:00.230
Okay.


00:09:05.573 --> 00:09:06.662
- It's you, isn't it?
- What?


00:09:06.693 --> 00:09:08.294
Doing all this.


00:09:08.902 --> 00:09:10.790
Come on, man,
we know that it's you.


00:09:10.821 --> 00:09:14.022
We done the forensics
on your spray cans.


00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.293
He's a joker, this one.
But, look, listen.


00:09:16.325 --> 00:09:18.245
I am Dodge,
this is Batesy,


00:09:18.277 --> 00:09:20.133
and together we...


00:09:27.078 --> 00:09:29.094
- What about your bikes?
- Not ours, pal!


00:09:36.677 --> 00:09:38.182
Come on!


00:09:41.317 --> 00:09:43.239
Hey! Stop!


00:09:48.293 --> 00:09:49.830
I said get down!


00:10:00.805 --> 00:10:03.302
Come on.


00:10:03.333 --> 00:10:05.541
- Cracking set of pins, love.
- Look at that.


00:10:05.573 --> 00:10:07.078
What happened to him?


00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:09.415
- What was that?
- Brilliant.


00:10:09.445 --> 00:10:11.078
You two again.


00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.702
Oh, come on.
We're your guardian angels.


00:10:13.734 --> 00:10:15.462
Where's the other guy?


00:10:15.494 --> 00:10:17.703
Come with us. We'll sort you out
with some new gear.


00:10:17.734 --> 00:10:20.454
Or you could just stay here.
I mean, it's up to you.


00:10:21.637 --> 00:10:23.206
We got trainers as well.


00:10:24.582 --> 00:10:26.118
Really?


00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:28.197
Come on, handsome.
Follow us.


00:10:32.742 --> 00:10:35.335
- I ain't got anything worth stealing.
- Come on, mate.


00:10:35.366 --> 00:10:37.990
You can't go through
life trusting no one.


00:10:38.022 --> 00:10:39.846
Yeah, we saved
your arse once already.


00:10:39.877 --> 00:10:41.542
That was
the other guy.


00:10:41.573 --> 00:10:43.493
What, you mean Red?


00:10:43.525 --> 00:10:45.383
Yeah.
The guy in the green jacket.


00:10:46.885 --> 00:10:49.030
That's a real hero,
that one.


00:10:58.214 --> 00:10:59.686
<i>Entre, s'il vous plaît.</i>


00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.357
<i>Who's that?</i>


00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.662
Just me and Batesy.


00:11:10.694 --> 00:11:12.263
What size waist are you?


00:11:12.294 --> 00:11:14.439
<i>I'd say he's about
a 30 regular.</i>


00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.166
Who's that?


00:11:16.196 --> 00:11:20.230
Oh, that is the ghost
of Dodge's grandpa.


00:11:20.262 --> 00:11:23.591
Batesy, shut up.
I'll introduce you later.


00:11:28.517 --> 00:11:30.341
Let's get you
some clobber first.


00:11:30.374 --> 00:11:32.006
Uh, you do realize
I've got no money?


00:11:32.038 --> 00:11:33.926
It's all right. You can owe us.


00:11:33.957 --> 00:11:35.718
I don't like
owing people.


00:11:38.309 --> 00:11:41.990
Go on, have 'em.
Introductory special offer.


00:11:42.405 --> 00:11:45.029
- We can spare 'em.
- Where did you get all this?


00:11:45.061 --> 00:11:47.942
- Sports Warehouse.
- Oh, I lost my favorite hat on that job.


00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:51.589
Are you ever gonna stop banging
on about that hat?


00:11:51.621 --> 00:11:53.542
- Huh?
- Probably not.


00:11:53.574 --> 00:11:57.605
Have 'em. They cost us nothing,
shop's claimed insurance.


00:11:57.638 --> 00:12:00.135
Plus, them pasty legs...


00:12:01.189 --> 00:12:03.141
they're gonna give me
nightmares.


00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.974
Oh, better give 'em a little bit
of a shake actually.


00:12:08.006 --> 00:12:10.279
Better give 'em
a shake first, eh.


00:12:15.173 --> 00:12:17.446
Hey, Fagin.


00:12:19.589 --> 00:12:22.470
Dodge, I've told you before.


00:12:22.502 --> 00:12:25.350
You cannot bring in green kids
off the street.


00:12:25.381 --> 00:12:27.525
- I know, but Fa...
- No buts.


00:12:27.557 --> 00:12:29.029
Out he goes.


00:12:29.061 --> 00:12:31.974
Fagin, please.
This is Twist.


00:12:32.454 --> 00:12:34.246
Extreme graffiti artist.


00:12:34.278 --> 00:12:35.910
Reaching places
others can't reach.


00:12:35.941 --> 00:12:37.862
Tags under moving cranes
and that.


00:12:37.894 --> 00:12:40.678
Like what's his face, uh...
Banksy. Yeah.


00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:43.431
Reaching places other people
can't reach, eh?


00:12:44.261 --> 00:12:47.622
The problem with graffiti is,
is you can't move it.


00:12:47.653 --> 00:12:50.343
What's the point in a painting
if it's always in the same place?


00:12:50.374 --> 00:12:53.254
The higher up I put my work,
the more people can see it.


00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.222
That's the point.
It doesn't belong to anybody.


00:12:57.253 --> 00:12:59.591
An idealist, eh?


00:12:59.621 --> 00:13:01.701
All property is theft.


00:13:02.341 --> 00:13:05.670
In my case,
that's literally true.


00:13:06.725 --> 00:13:09.317
Tell me, Mr. Idealist,


00:13:09.861 --> 00:13:12.166
how's virtue treating you?


00:13:12.198 --> 00:13:14.277
Is it filling your stomach?


00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.518
Can it give you
a hug on a cold night?


00:13:16.549 --> 00:13:19.878
Ideals are useless.
They're like appendix.


00:13:20.965 --> 00:13:22.213
Cut 'em out.


00:13:22.245 --> 00:13:23.365
He's fast.


00:13:23.398 --> 00:13:25.734
He left the Old Bill for dust.


00:13:25.765 --> 00:13:28.101
I thought maybe
we could train him up


00:13:28.134 --> 00:13:30.438
seeing as
we have a vacancy.


00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:31.877
I'm not a thief.


00:13:31.909 --> 00:13:34.822
What, you've never stole
a sarnie from Tescos?


00:13:34.853 --> 00:13:38.117
I don't need to. They chuck out
enough if you know where to look.


00:13:38.149 --> 00:13:40.229
Oh, living the dream.


00:13:40.261 --> 00:13:42.565
We all have to start somewhere,
don't we?


00:13:42.597 --> 00:13:45.446
It wasn't so long ago that you
were stealing credit card details.


00:13:45.478 --> 00:13:46.917
Uh, it's called phishing.


00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:49.093
It's called surviving.


00:13:49.126 --> 00:13:52.006
It's what we do
to survive.


00:13:52.933 --> 00:13:55.398
- Suppose.
- Bravo.


00:13:55.429 --> 00:13:56.774
You need a place to stay?


00:13:59.462 --> 00:14:00.614
No. Thank you.


00:14:01.446 --> 00:14:04.134
Cheers for the clothes.
I'll pay you back.


00:14:08.837 --> 00:14:11.077
That's
a really decent copy.


00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:13.926
I've seen the original tons
of times at the Tate.


00:14:13.956 --> 00:14:15.078
No, you haven't.


00:14:21.798 --> 00:14:24.262
I tell you what.
I'll cook tonight, Dodge.


00:14:24.293 --> 00:14:26.405
What do you want,
spaghetti or beef burgers?


00:14:26.436 --> 00:14:28.037
- I love the...
- Ah, nah.


00:14:28.069 --> 00:14:29.509
Come on. Do me a flavor, Fag.


00:14:29.541 --> 00:14:32.293
You know I'm 72% vegan.
Meat is a treat.


00:14:32.325 --> 00:14:35.685
Doesn't matter what you eat
so long as you eat together.


00:14:35.718 --> 00:14:38.886
Because, as I've always said,
the most important thing


00:14:38.917 --> 00:14:41.445
is the family
that eats together...


00:14:41.477 --> 00:14:43.397
...stays together.


00:14:43.429 --> 00:14:45.190
Yeah. Right.


00:14:54.021 --> 00:14:56.037
Oi! Mate.


00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:58.630
I just wanted to...


00:15:00.006 --> 00:15:01.510
Stand there gawping
like a fish?


00:15:02.245 --> 00:15:04.453
If you could speak sometime
soon that'd be great


00:15:04.484 --> 00:15:05.957
- 'cause I've got somewhere to go.
- I'm sorry.


00:15:05.988 --> 00:15:07.813
I didn't realize you,
you were a...


00:15:07.846 --> 00:15:09.413
And I didn't recognize you
with clothes on.


00:15:09.446 --> 00:15:10.885
I just wanted to say thanks.


00:15:10.917 --> 00:15:12.486
You're welcome.


00:15:13.605 --> 00:15:15.045
Is that everything?


00:15:16.646 --> 00:15:18.214
I'll take that as a yes.


00:16:45.476 --> 00:16:47.397
The boy's an artist.


00:16:47.429 --> 00:16:49.318
So, what do you see?


00:16:49.349 --> 00:16:52.005
A loner with a cracking pair
of trainers?


00:16:52.934 --> 00:16:55.366
Well, that's disappointing.
You missed the point.


00:16:58.021 --> 00:16:59.942
Can you get up there?


00:16:59.973 --> 00:17:01.957
Please. If he can...


00:17:02.598 --> 00:17:05.062
- Yeah.
- Some boys like respect.


00:17:05.893 --> 00:17:09.317
Some boys like being
in the pecking order.


00:17:09.349 --> 00:17:10.566
But this one...


00:17:11.174 --> 00:17:13.636
he wants something
that he's missing.


00:17:13.668 --> 00:17:15.110
A smartphone?


00:17:17.476 --> 00:17:18.917
He wants love.


00:17:18.949 --> 00:17:21.094
So let's give it
to him.


00:17:55.653 --> 00:17:57.734
Glad I climbed up
this side.


00:17:57.765 --> 00:17:58.853
Sorry!


00:17:58.886 --> 00:18:00.999
There's no toilet
up here.


00:18:01.478 --> 00:18:03.238
Love what you've done
with the place.


00:18:03.269 --> 00:18:05.478
It's just while
I'm doing this one here.


00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.733
Gonna offer me
a cup of tea then, or...


00:18:09.765 --> 00:18:12.166
I could do you cream crackers
and chocolate spread.


00:18:12.196 --> 00:18:13.830
Ooh, nutritious.


00:18:15.716 --> 00:18:17.637
I thought you were
a guy, by the way.


00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:19.494
That's why I was being
weird earlier.


00:18:19.524 --> 00:18:20.741
You say
the sweetest things.


00:18:20.772 --> 00:18:23.205
No, no. I wasn't...


00:18:23.238 --> 00:18:25.670
I mean, I just...


00:18:25.702 --> 00:18:29.125
- The way you move...
- Like a guy? Yeah. I get it.


00:18:29.862 --> 00:18:32.902
- I don't mean to offend you.
- Oh, why would that offend me?


00:18:32.933 --> 00:18:34.053
Just guys are more strong.


00:18:34.724 --> 00:18:36.549
Not that girls aren't strong.


00:18:36.582 --> 00:18:38.054
Girls are strong as well.


00:18:38.086 --> 00:18:39.974
Just guys tend to be...
I don't know.


00:18:40.006 --> 00:18:41.989
Not much of
a smooth talker, are we?


00:18:42.597 --> 00:18:44.358
Best stick to climbing
I think.


00:18:46.182 --> 00:18:47.814
How come you're so good
at climbing anyway?


00:18:51.396 --> 00:18:54.245
When I was younger,
I felt safer up high.


00:18:55.396 --> 00:18:56.998
People couldn't find me.


00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.901
So I taught myself
to climb.


00:19:01.381 --> 00:19:03.526
And you've been a loner
on a roof ever since?


00:19:04.196 --> 00:19:05.957
Suits me just fine.


00:19:07.301 --> 00:19:08.805
Well, you can't stay
up here forever.


00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:11.749
Isn't there things you wanna
see, things you wanna experience?


00:19:11.782 --> 00:19:13.414
Must get pretty boring.


00:19:13.445 --> 00:19:15.046
I can go anywhere I want.


00:19:16.549 --> 00:19:17.894
- What?
- See.


00:19:30.821 --> 00:19:32.262
I can imagine.


00:19:32.293 --> 00:19:35.301
Well, I'm here
in real life,


00:19:35.716 --> 00:19:38.405
and I've come to invite you
to a real-life dinner.


00:19:38.436 --> 00:19:40.005
Me and you?


00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:44.357
Come to Fagin's,
tonight at 7:00.


00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:46.853
And you never know,


00:19:46.885 --> 00:19:49.479
we might just be better
company than your paintings.


00:20:25.414 --> 00:20:26.694
What am I doing?


00:20:26.726 --> 00:20:28.389
What does Oliver see?


00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:31.302
Mum?


00:20:35.684 --> 00:20:37.093
Can't be by yourself forever.


00:20:42.341 --> 00:20:44.484
You're late.


00:20:44.516 --> 00:20:46.757
Is that any way to greet
your favorite supplier?


00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.133
What happened to Tom?


00:20:52.676 --> 00:20:54.533
He screwed up.
That's what happened.


00:20:55.366 --> 00:20:58.214
My kids are not disposable.


00:20:58.246 --> 00:21:00.806
That's exactly what they are,
my old friend.


00:21:01.541 --> 00:21:04.357
No friends, no family.
No questions.


00:21:12.164 --> 00:21:14.117
For complications.


00:21:20.452 --> 00:21:22.692
Did you get my envelope?


00:21:22.725 --> 00:21:24.230
What, this?


00:21:26.021 --> 00:21:27.654
When has it ever been
that easy, eh?


00:21:29.028 --> 00:21:30.468
I want in.


00:21:30.501 --> 00:21:32.389
I know you're pulling
a job.


00:21:32.421 --> 00:21:34.213
You're hitting Losberne.


00:21:34.692 --> 00:21:36.324
I want a cut.


00:21:36.357 --> 00:21:37.540
I was gonna tell you.


00:21:37.573 --> 00:21:38.726
Of course you were.


00:21:38.756 --> 00:21:40.485
Let me make it
easy for you.


00:21:40.517 --> 00:21:41.862
Whatever's in there...


00:21:42.949 --> 00:21:44.805
seems very important
to your little plan.


00:21:44.837 --> 00:21:47.077
Question is, are we gonna do it
the easy or the hard way?


00:21:56.805 --> 00:21:58.373
Partners.


00:22:05.285 --> 00:22:07.813
Partners. Now...


00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:10.629
the envelope.


00:22:11.652 --> 00:22:12.837
I think I'll keep it.


00:22:13.925 --> 00:22:16.358
Just in case
of future complications.


00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:35.974
Yeah.


00:22:36.004 --> 00:22:39.621
Took your bloody...
Oh, my giddy aunt.


00:22:39.653 --> 00:22:41.989
What is happening
with your barnet?


00:22:42.021 --> 00:22:44.485
Sorry.
Sorry, sorry, sorry.


00:22:44.516 --> 00:22:47.206
Come on, look, look.
Welcome, Twist.


00:22:47.237 --> 00:22:51.558
Let me take your jean shirt,
jacket for you. There we go.


00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:54.917
- Come on.
- Ah.


00:22:54.948 --> 00:22:56.772
Glad you could make it,
mate.


00:22:56.805 --> 00:22:59.269
Oh, Twist.
Come and sit next to me.


00:23:02.854 --> 00:23:05.957
Oh, blimey, look. Nancy,
take his beautiful flowers


00:23:05.989 --> 00:23:07.270
and put them in some water.


00:23:08.613 --> 00:23:09.733
Mmm.


00:23:12.389 --> 00:23:14.052
He can call me that.


00:23:14.085 --> 00:23:15.365
- You don't.
- Understood.


00:23:15.397 --> 00:23:18.821
I am starving.


00:23:18.853 --> 00:23:20.261
Dodge, please.


00:23:20.293 --> 00:23:22.022
Fagin, can we just
talk about something?


00:23:22.054 --> 00:23:24.230
Can we talk about our boy,
Batesy here,


00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:26.085
stealing my food
from under my bed?


00:23:26.116 --> 00:23:28.036
- Grass.
- Thief.


00:23:28.068 --> 00:23:30.694
- Okay, we're all thieves.
- Yeah, be a better one is the point.


00:23:30.724 --> 00:23:32.836
All right. Okay, okay.


00:23:32.869 --> 00:23:35.110
Uh, Twist,


00:23:35.141 --> 00:23:38.564
I want you to say a few words
because it's a tradition.


00:23:38.597 --> 00:23:41.126
About how thankful you are.


00:23:42.436 --> 00:23:46.117
Well, thanks for having me
round for dinner, I suppose.


00:23:46.149 --> 00:23:48.869
I can't remember the last time
that I sat down...


00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:50.566
Like a family?


00:23:51.589 --> 00:23:53.606
We're all orphans here.


00:23:59.301 --> 00:24:00.710
All right,
that's the thanks.


00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.373
Cool, um,
can we bloody eat now?


00:24:02.405 --> 00:24:04.454
- Yes! Eat. Eat.
- All right!


00:24:04.484 --> 00:24:06.404
- Eat.
- All right, all right.


00:24:06.437 --> 00:24:08.198
Let's go.


00:24:08.228 --> 00:24:09.702
Mmm.


00:24:17.925 --> 00:24:20.326
It appears that
you're a connoisseur of beauty.


00:24:20.997 --> 00:24:25.638
Yeah. I saw you in my office
admiring my collection, Mr. Twist.


00:24:26.725 --> 00:24:28.645
Can I stop using that name?


00:24:28.677 --> 00:24:31.013
It makes me sound
as though I'm in a casino.


00:24:32.004 --> 00:24:33.284
What else can I call you?


00:24:34.085 --> 00:24:35.108
Oliver.


00:24:35.140 --> 00:24:37.764
Oliver. Well, Oliver,


00:24:37.796 --> 00:24:40.100
your artwork is impressive.


00:24:40.133 --> 00:24:41.798
They're just copies.


00:24:41.829 --> 00:24:44.485
No, nothing is just a copy.
We always put a little bit


00:24:44.516 --> 00:24:46.533
of soul into everything,
don't you think?


00:24:47.749 --> 00:24:50.213
- Yeah, I suppose.
- When I was your age,


00:24:50.244 --> 00:24:52.293
I wanted to be an artist,
just like you.


00:24:52.773 --> 00:24:55.045
But my father was tasteless.
A bully.


00:24:55.076 --> 00:24:56.806
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:24:56.836 --> 00:24:59.685
Why sorry?
This is all my art, and Nancy...


00:25:00.868 --> 00:25:02.501
is my masterpiece.


00:25:02.917 --> 00:25:04.997
She needs someone to train with.


00:25:05.029 --> 00:25:07.301
Someone who can keep up
with her.


00:25:08.068 --> 00:25:12.228
- So you all just do whatever you want?
- Yes. But together.


00:25:12.261 --> 00:25:13.700
We never work alone.


00:25:13.732 --> 00:25:17.284
You know, we live together,
we eat together.


00:25:17.316 --> 00:25:19.044
Because the family
that eats together...


00:25:19.077 --> 00:25:20.932
Stays together. I know.


00:25:23.108 --> 00:25:24.197
Watch this,
watch this.


00:25:25.189 --> 00:25:27.014
Got a little surprise
for you.


00:25:27.044 --> 00:25:28.549
- For me?
- Yeah.


00:25:38.597 --> 00:25:39.909
Come on, then.


00:25:40.517 --> 00:25:42.853
You ready?
We're going out.


00:25:43.396 --> 00:25:44.998
Come on.


00:25:45.028 --> 00:25:47.877
Make sure you bring him back
in one piece.


00:25:58.277 --> 00:26:00.069
Don't you guys
ever feel bad?


00:26:00.645 --> 00:26:03.077
What? No.


00:26:03.109 --> 00:26:05.477
Look, the people that
we target are criminals anyway.


00:26:05.508 --> 00:26:08.198
So, it's justified,
innit?


00:26:08.228 --> 00:26:11.108
Think of Fagin
as good old Robin Hood


00:26:11.141 --> 00:26:12.773
and we're his Merry Men.


00:26:12.804 --> 00:26:14.053
Hmm.


00:26:40.741 --> 00:26:42.278
Oliver.


00:26:43.397 --> 00:26:44.644
Oliver.


00:26:44.677 --> 00:26:47.078
Hey, wake up. Come on.


00:26:48.485 --> 00:26:50.406
Get changed.
We're going out.


00:26:52.453 --> 00:26:53.893
Okay, give me a sec.


00:26:59.717 --> 00:27:02.214
- So, are you sticking around?
- Yeah, I think I will.


00:27:02.245 --> 00:27:04.069
You sure
you wanna do this?


00:27:04.101 --> 00:27:06.885
Yeah. It's nice
to belong to something.


00:27:07.749 --> 00:27:09.317
Trust me, you'll be fine.


00:27:22.821 --> 00:27:24.229
Morning, Dr. Losberne.


00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:27.685
Good morning.


00:27:31.589 --> 00:27:34.693
Dr. Crispin Losberne.


00:27:36.644 --> 00:27:38.661
Curator, art dealer


00:27:38.692 --> 00:27:42.244
and connoisseur
of 18th-century painters.


00:27:42.277 --> 00:27:44.805
He's very predictable,
which helps.


00:27:44.836 --> 00:27:50.053
Gets up every morning and leaves
for work at eight o'clock sharp.


00:27:50.085 --> 00:27:52.709
<i>He looks at his messages</i>


00:27:52.741 --> 00:27:56.645
<i>and he puts his phone away in the
right-hand pocket of his coat.</i>


00:27:56.676 --> 00:27:59.588
- Flat white.
- <i>Pays the barista.</i>


00:27:59.621 --> 00:28:01.445
Then he drinks his coffee.


00:28:01.477 --> 00:28:03.237
- Hmm.
- What's all this about?


00:28:03.268 --> 00:28:05.540
Well, we're gonna borrow
his phone.


00:28:05.572 --> 00:28:08.485
And have it back in his pocket
before he knows it's gone.


00:28:08.516 --> 00:28:09.956
But why?


00:28:09.989 --> 00:28:11.781
He took everything from me.


00:28:11.813 --> 00:28:12.997
Everything.


00:28:14.692 --> 00:28:17.476
And I'm going
to return the favor.


00:28:17.987 --> 00:28:21.253
First thing, we need
to hack Losberne's phone.


00:28:21.829 --> 00:28:24.133
Oh, and as far as the day
is concerned,


00:28:24.164 --> 00:28:25.604
it's all performance art.


00:28:25.637 --> 00:28:29.030
And the performance
will be given by Nancy.


00:28:31.428 --> 00:28:32.710
Oh!


00:28:32.740 --> 00:28:34.052
I am such a klutz.


00:28:34.085 --> 00:28:36.004
Let me help.
I've got tissues in my bag.


00:28:36.037 --> 00:28:37.510
You absolutely must
let me help.


00:28:37.541 --> 00:28:39.909
God, it's all over
your lovely jacket.


00:28:39.941 --> 00:28:41.350
Oh, I'm so stupid.


00:28:46.276 --> 00:28:47.780
I was on my way
to the Royal Academy


00:28:47.813 --> 00:28:49.285
to see
the Gainsborough exhibition.


00:28:49.316 --> 00:28:51.013
- Really.
- Oh, have you been?


00:28:53.605 --> 00:28:55.525
As a matter of fact,
I curated it.


00:28:55.556 --> 00:28:58.373
- Really?
- Oh, yes. Come on.


00:28:58.404 --> 00:29:00.614
- <i>Dodge, you got it yet?</i>
- Yeah, plugging in.


00:29:01.668 --> 00:29:04.964
All right.
On its way, Batesy.


00:29:04.996 --> 00:29:07.269
I'm quite a mover and shaker
in the art world.


00:29:07.300 --> 00:29:08.325
I have my own place.


00:29:08.357 --> 00:29:09.606
You have
your own gallery?


00:29:10.565 --> 00:29:12.228
<i>That working, Bates?</i>


00:29:12.260 --> 00:29:14.342
You don't ever need interns,
do you?


00:29:14.373 --> 00:29:15.492
Never say never.


00:29:17.221 --> 00:29:18.533
<i>Come on, Batesy.
Hurry up.</i>


00:29:18.564 --> 00:29:20.197
I'll give you my card.


00:29:20.229 --> 00:29:22.277
<i>I'm going as quick as I can.</i>


00:29:22.307 --> 00:29:23.589
It's in my jacket.


00:29:23.621 --> 00:29:24.773
Oh.


00:29:26.533 --> 00:29:28.069
<i>We need
to speed this up.</i>


00:29:28.101 --> 00:29:30.501
Yes, of course.


00:29:32.356 --> 00:29:33.765
- Oh.
- Bit wet.


00:29:33.796 --> 00:29:35.492
Hurry up,
hurry up, hurry up.


00:29:35.525 --> 00:29:37.125
Pop by anytime.


00:29:38.117 --> 00:29:40.838
- Goodbye.
- Dodge, quick, he's leaving.


00:29:45.220 --> 00:29:46.342
Quickly!


00:29:46.789 --> 00:29:48.262
Yes. Let's go.


00:29:55.044 --> 00:29:56.933
Garages on Swift Road.


00:30:06.437 --> 00:30:08.166
Someone's taken my phone.


00:30:22.468 --> 00:30:23.620
Get out of my taxi!


00:30:23.652 --> 00:30:25.702
Sorry, mate.
I thought it was free.


00:30:27.716 --> 00:30:29.444
- God.
- Is that what you're looking for?


00:30:31.269 --> 00:30:33.670
Yes. Thank you.


00:30:33.700 --> 00:30:36.068
You can keep the taxi.
I'm going to walk.


00:30:36.101 --> 00:30:37.893
Cheers.


00:30:40.997 --> 00:30:42.501
Where to, guv?


00:30:44.580 --> 00:30:46.245
Not bad for your first job,
Oliver.


00:30:46.276 --> 00:30:48.452
Yeah, and that was just
the hors d'oeuvre.


00:30:49.189 --> 00:30:52.196
Batesy, keep hacking.


00:30:52.229 --> 00:30:55.141
One word from Losberne,
I wanna hear it.


00:30:55.173 --> 00:30:57.734
We need to know his every move.


00:30:58.404 --> 00:30:59.908
- Dodge?
- Yeah?


00:30:59.941 --> 00:31:01.252
Do the washing up.


00:31:01.285 --> 00:31:03.461
Oh, man.


00:31:03.492 --> 00:31:05.764
Nancy, you're going
to art school.


00:31:05.796 --> 00:31:07.269
What?


00:31:07.300 --> 00:31:09.381
It's a crash course.


00:31:09.412 --> 00:31:11.748
If you're gonna be convincing
as an art student


00:31:11.781 --> 00:31:13.605
for an evening,
or even for ten minutes,


00:31:13.636 --> 00:31:16.036
you're gonna have to know
some art to talk about.


00:31:16.932 --> 00:31:18.916
Oliver, would you mind?


00:31:18.948 --> 00:31:20.773
- Of course.
- Ah, good.


00:31:21.222 --> 00:31:23.333
But nothing beats seeing
it in the flesh.


00:31:24.836 --> 00:31:26.757
This is about
Pope Nicholas.


00:31:27.493 --> 00:31:29.029
He's fuming.


00:31:29.061 --> 00:31:30.852
And Dante's... Shit.


00:31:31.525 --> 00:31:32.581
Wha...


00:31:32.964 --> 00:31:34.501
Guard.


00:31:35.300 --> 00:31:37.156
You do realize
this gallery's free, yeah?


00:31:37.188 --> 00:31:39.428
He's worked here
for years. He hates me.


00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:41.412
He's always throwing me out
for sleeping here.


00:31:42.852 --> 00:31:45.221
Get up.
Here, I got you.


00:31:46.757 --> 00:31:48.133
He doesn't scare me.


00:31:51.045 --> 00:31:52.581
Shall we...


00:32:02.276 --> 00:32:03.622
Millais's a genius.


00:32:04.582 --> 00:32:08.101
- The use of...
- Hardly gonna win the 500-meter backstroke, though, is she?


00:32:10.019 --> 00:32:11.750
I'm joking.
I know it's Ophelia.


00:32:12.900 --> 00:32:14.501
Anything else
you'd like to add?


00:32:16.067 --> 00:32:17.860
Well, personally,


00:32:17.891 --> 00:32:19.396
I think the flowers
in the painting


00:32:19.429 --> 00:32:21.317
are as important
as Ophelia herself.


00:32:21.828 --> 00:32:24.164
The floating flowers,
they represent her sorrow.


00:32:24.197 --> 00:32:26.437
And the nettles growing
around the willow,


00:32:26.468 --> 00:32:28.069
well that's...
that's her pain.


00:32:29.220 --> 00:32:30.949
Exactly.


00:32:30.980 --> 00:32:32.709
Did you do art
at school?


00:32:32.740 --> 00:32:35.844
No. It's just
common sense, innit?


00:32:35.876 --> 00:32:38.501
Well, that
and the Internet.


00:32:38.533 --> 00:32:40.741
All right.
Let's see what else you got.


00:32:50.020 --> 00:32:53.381
So, do you feel ready to be the most
convincing art student of all time?


00:32:53.412 --> 00:32:55.813
Yeah. Totally.


00:32:55.844 --> 00:32:57.924
Although no thanks
to my teacher. He was rubbish.


00:32:57.955 --> 00:32:59.268
Oi!


00:33:00.869 --> 00:33:02.022
So, uh...


00:33:03.172 --> 00:33:05.125
couldn't help
but notice old Ophelia


00:33:05.157 --> 00:33:06.885
made quite an impression
on you in there.


00:33:07.715 --> 00:33:09.254
Yeah.


00:33:10.372 --> 00:33:11.748
What was it about her?


00:33:15.428 --> 00:33:17.381
I used to go to
that gallery with my mum.


00:33:18.467 --> 00:33:19.812
She was an artist.


00:33:19.844 --> 00:33:22.276
Right.
That makes sense.


00:33:23.717 --> 00:33:25.989
- So, you did have a family?
- Just a mum.


00:33:27.204 --> 00:33:29.062
She wasn't around
for too long.


00:33:30.629 --> 00:33:32.357
Did you?


00:33:32.389 --> 00:33:33.860
Just a dad.


00:33:33.891 --> 00:33:35.588
But he was around
for too long.


00:33:38.627 --> 00:33:40.421
So why did you get
into free running then?


00:33:41.956 --> 00:33:43.206
So I could escape.


00:33:44.004 --> 00:33:45.349
Escape from what?


00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:49.508
From boys called
Oliver Twist.


00:33:55.076 --> 00:33:56.516
Come here!


00:33:57.700 --> 00:34:02.213
<i>To pull this job off, we'll
need the plans for Losberne's gallery.</i>


00:34:03.460 --> 00:34:05.380
<i>Oh, not
the caterpillar tash.</i>


00:34:05.411 --> 00:34:06.980
- Hello.
- Good morning, sir.


00:34:07.013 --> 00:34:08.741
We spoke on the telephone


00:34:08.773 --> 00:34:11.717
about your conversion
of number 30.


00:34:11.748 --> 00:34:13.188
The Losberne Gallery?


00:34:13.221 --> 00:34:15.877
I have bought
the building opposite


00:34:15.909 --> 00:34:19.844
and I want you to make it modern
like number 30.


00:34:19.876 --> 00:34:22.756
I have the plans here. I can show
you what we did for Dr. Losberne.


00:34:22.787 --> 00:34:24.420
Follow me.


00:34:26.981 --> 00:34:29.828
Yes. Very nice,
very nice.


00:34:32.868 --> 00:34:33.861
<i>Da.</i>


00:34:33.892 --> 00:34:36.804
11:05 on the dot, Fagin.


00:34:36.835 --> 00:34:38.468
Just like you said.


00:34:49.605 --> 00:34:51.493
This is private.


00:34:51.525 --> 00:34:54.021
It's okay.
I don't understand Russian, so...


00:34:55.525 --> 00:34:57.125
You want my business?


00:34:58.052 --> 00:35:00.549
Certainly.
Take your time.


00:35:00.580 --> 00:35:01.988
Thank you.


00:35:12.101 --> 00:35:15.173
No windows, reinforced walls.


00:35:16.164 --> 00:35:17.157
That's the one.


00:35:17.731 --> 00:35:19.844
That'll be
a job getting in.


00:35:19.876 --> 00:35:21.381
We don't have to do that.


00:35:21.924 --> 00:35:24.644
If we do
what I've got planned,


00:35:25.125 --> 00:35:26.693
they bring it out.


00:35:26.724 --> 00:35:28.036
Batesy, carry on.


00:35:28.067 --> 00:35:29.445
Bring what out?


00:35:30.021 --> 00:35:33.604
This is the painting
we're gonna steal.


00:35:33.636 --> 00:35:36.773
One of six paintings
by William Hogarth.


00:35:36.805 --> 00:35:39.493
That says Dotheboy's
Auction House, Fagin.


00:35:39.524 --> 00:35:41.060
Why are we casing up Losberne?


00:35:41.093 --> 00:35:42.885
The painting
was lost in a fire,


00:35:42.917 --> 00:35:45.828
but many people believed
it was a cover-up for a theft.


00:35:45.860 --> 00:35:49.029
All this time,
it's been off the radar.


00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:51.781
So you're saying
Losberne's got it?


00:35:51.813 --> 00:35:53.892
- He's the seller.
- Wait, hang about.


00:35:53.924 --> 00:35:55.460
How did he get his hands on it?


00:35:55.492 --> 00:35:58.533
Many years ago,
Losberne went into partnership


00:35:58.564 --> 00:36:00.612
with a man called
Isaac Solomon.


00:36:00.644 --> 00:36:03.044
Both of them bought
a lot of paintings.


00:36:03.076 --> 00:36:05.444
One of them was the Hogarth.


00:36:05.475 --> 00:36:07.299
But when they had it in auction,


00:36:07.331 --> 00:36:11.044
Losberne went missing
with the paintings.


00:36:11.075 --> 00:36:13.540
- Oh.
- And Solomon had nothing,


00:36:13.572 --> 00:36:16.740
and his credibility
as an art dealer was gone.


00:36:17.220 --> 00:36:20.773
Later, Losberne said
the paintings had been stolen.


00:36:20.805 --> 00:36:22.180
So my man tells me.


00:36:23.044 --> 00:36:25.605
How long have you been there?
I didn't hear you come in.


00:36:25.636 --> 00:36:27.236
You should be more careful,
Fagin.


00:36:27.268 --> 00:36:28.996
You're getting sloppy
in your old age.


00:36:32.900 --> 00:36:34.373
Oh,
it's only you two.


00:36:34.405 --> 00:36:37.829
Oliver, there's someone
I'd like you to meet.


00:36:39.587 --> 00:36:40.580
Oliver.


00:36:43.045 --> 00:36:44.325
Here, boy.


00:36:44.805 --> 00:36:46.564
This is Bullseye.


00:36:46.596 --> 00:36:47.652
Aw...


00:36:48.131 --> 00:36:50.372
You're gonna need
your hands later.


00:36:52.195 --> 00:36:53.828
Round two.


00:36:56.292 --> 00:36:57.829
Magnetic, see?


00:36:58.244 --> 00:37:00.004
Stick it on a pipe and get out.


00:37:10.596 --> 00:37:12.356
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Is it a bad time?


00:37:13.604 --> 00:37:15.012
It's the perfect time.


00:37:25.155 --> 00:37:26.884
Thank you.


00:37:27.843 --> 00:37:28.836
Bottoms up.


00:37:28.869 --> 00:37:30.277
Oh.


00:37:31.012 --> 00:37:32.421
Cheers.


00:37:38.147 --> 00:37:40.067
So, you were saying
it'd be answering the phones,


00:37:40.099 --> 00:37:41.891
doing a little bit of filing?


00:37:41.923 --> 00:37:44.260
Nothing a girl
like you couldn't handle.


00:37:44.837 --> 00:37:47.557
I did actually want
to show you some of my art.


00:37:48.292 --> 00:37:49.733
Street art, you say?


00:37:49.764 --> 00:37:51.557
Yeah,
it's just on here.


00:37:55.397 --> 00:37:56.932
<i>Let me just find them.</i>


00:37:57.604 --> 00:37:59.173
<i>Uh, yes. Okay.</i>


00:37:59.780 --> 00:38:01.125
This one is actually
based on...


00:38:01.156 --> 00:38:03.044
William Blake.
Of course.


00:38:05.156 --> 00:38:07.268
I love what you've done
with the line there.


00:38:08.420 --> 00:38:10.692
<i>These are actually
rather intriguing.</i>


00:38:10.724 --> 00:38:11.780
<i>Don't gas me.</i>


00:38:13.220 --> 00:38:14.756
Come on, girl.


00:38:14.787 --> 00:38:15.973
Give her a second.


00:38:16.004 --> 00:38:17.924
Sorry,
that's my graffiti talk.


00:38:17.956 --> 00:38:20.229
It's the only way to get taken
seriously on the street.


00:38:21.603 --> 00:38:23.237
Oh, right.


00:38:23.267 --> 00:38:25.061
Well, don't forget
your wine.


00:38:25.092 --> 00:38:27.107
Do you know, it's just going
straight through me.


00:38:27.139 --> 00:38:29.060
I must pop to
the little girls' room.


00:38:35.268 --> 00:38:36.741
Is it downstairs, or...


00:38:37.732 --> 00:38:39.012
Straight down
the stairs.


00:38:39.044 --> 00:38:40.516
The door straight
in front of you.


00:38:42.723 --> 00:38:44.612
Okay. Thanks.


00:39:00.068 --> 00:39:02.788
Oh, no. No, no, no.
He's on the move.


00:39:11.236 --> 00:39:13.988
- <i>I could have blown my hand off.</i>
- Yeah, calm down.


00:39:14.021 --> 00:39:16.260
- Everything all right?
- Yes, I'll be up in a minute.


00:39:16.293 --> 00:39:18.117
You better have brought
a spare.


00:39:18.148 --> 00:39:19.141
Uh...


00:39:23.109 --> 00:39:24.837
We just gotta get it
to her.


00:39:24.868 --> 00:39:25.893
I'll take it.


00:39:26.276 --> 00:39:27.717
I'm the climber,
right?


00:39:27.747 --> 00:39:30.020
Whatever you do,
don't drop it.


00:40:02.468 --> 00:40:04.356
Red, it's me.
Let me in.


00:40:08.292 --> 00:40:09.669
Look out.


00:40:10.947 --> 00:40:12.741
- Oh, my God.
- Be careful.


00:40:12.772 --> 00:40:14.148
Okay...


00:40:16.900 --> 00:40:18.564
What's going on
down there?


00:40:28.676 --> 00:40:29.956
Losberne Gallery.


00:40:29.988 --> 00:40:31.173
Special delivery.


00:40:31.204 --> 00:40:32.900
At this time of night?


00:40:32.932 --> 00:40:34.948
I'm right outside, mate.
Got a large package.


00:40:34.979 --> 00:40:37.571
Says, "artworks, fragile."


00:40:37.603 --> 00:40:39.876
I could leave it
on the doorstep if you want?


00:40:39.908 --> 00:40:41.476
No, no, no.
I'm coming. I'm coming.


00:40:41.508 --> 00:40:43.365
I was just in
the middle of something.


00:40:43.396 --> 00:40:44.516
One second.


00:40:45.027 --> 00:40:47.493
I'm at the window.
Where are you?


00:40:47.523 --> 00:40:49.572
<i>Um, let me
just check on that.</i>


00:40:49.604 --> 00:40:51.365
Sorry, mate. Wrong number.


00:41:01.923 --> 00:41:05.571
I wouldn't use that lav...
uh, bathroom for a bit.


00:41:06.404 --> 00:41:08.804
I'm sorry. You're going to have
to wait here for a moment.


00:41:08.836 --> 00:41:10.341
Brittles?


00:41:10.371 --> 00:41:11.812
Can you come up here, please?


00:41:20.133 --> 00:41:21.701
What is this?


00:41:25.668 --> 00:41:27.428
Search her bag.


00:41:27.972 --> 00:41:28.997
Hey!


00:41:29.667 --> 00:41:30.883
Excuse me!


00:41:35.684 --> 00:41:37.444
If that's the way
you treat all your interns,


00:41:37.475 --> 00:41:38.724
you can take
your work experience


00:41:38.755 --> 00:41:40.165
and shove it up your arse!


00:42:01.667 --> 00:42:03.300
Okay.


00:42:26.980 --> 00:42:30.052
<i>Our Dr. Losberne is gonna
get a surprise in the morning.</i>


00:42:30.083 --> 00:42:32.227
Until then,
you can take the night off.


00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:34.628
- Go out, have some fun.
- Yes!


00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:36.675
Yeah, but wait a minute.
Not too much fun


00:42:36.708 --> 00:42:39.076
because you're back
on duty at 7:00 a.m.


00:42:39.108 --> 00:42:40.163
7:00?


00:42:40.195 --> 00:42:42.019
We've all gotta be ready


00:42:42.052 --> 00:42:43.813
to move when
the phone goes.


00:42:43.843 --> 00:42:45.828
And I'll stay tuned to Losberne.


00:42:45.859 --> 00:42:49.028
Well, you know he might be
into some heavy phone sex,


00:42:49.060 --> 00:42:51.620
which means you might be in
for a steamy night, old boy.


00:42:51.651 --> 00:42:53.508
So there's this party.


00:42:53.540 --> 00:42:55.268
- What you saying?
- Red, you coming?


00:42:55.300 --> 00:42:56.740
She got plans.


00:43:00.900 --> 00:43:02.468
You did good.


00:43:15.331 --> 00:43:17.028
Mate, let's go.
Come on.


00:43:17.636 --> 00:43:18.981
Awkward.


00:43:33.540 --> 00:43:36.676
Come on, mate. Don't be such
a Debbie Downer.


00:43:36.707 --> 00:43:39.268
You know, there are
other birds in London.


00:43:39.748 --> 00:43:41.572
Come on.
Have a drink with us.


00:43:41.603 --> 00:43:43.940
No, I'm all right, mate.
Honestly.


00:43:43.971 --> 00:43:45.923
Come on.
You know you want to.


00:43:45.955 --> 00:43:47.204
Seriously, Batesy.


00:43:47.684 --> 00:43:49.061
I'm all right here.


00:43:49.923 --> 00:43:51.459
All right. Fine.


00:44:00.164 --> 00:44:01.733
- Hey.
- I said...


00:44:02.724 --> 00:44:05.028
Oi. You mug.


00:44:06.340 --> 00:44:07.812
She belongs to Sikes.


00:44:07.843 --> 00:44:09.700
You think
I don't know that?


00:44:09.731 --> 00:44:10.885
I don't belong to anyone.


00:44:18.691 --> 00:44:19.717
We'll see.


00:44:47.651 --> 00:44:50.084
Oi, Batesy!
Batesy, look out!


00:45:01.123 --> 00:45:03.172
I love coming here.


00:45:03.203 --> 00:45:05.092
You almost forget
you're in the city.


00:45:05.604 --> 00:45:07.684
How do you know
about this place?


00:45:07.715 --> 00:45:10.596
Uh, Sikes brought me
here once.


00:45:12.291 --> 00:45:13.700
Why'd you bring me
here then?


00:45:14.691 --> 00:45:17.796
Because I wanted to.
Is that okay?


00:45:18.979 --> 00:45:20.260
Hmm?


00:45:26.788 --> 00:45:28.548
Red!


00:45:40.036 --> 00:45:41.987
Seriously, why did
you bring me here?


00:45:42.019 --> 00:45:43.876
Why wouldn't
I bring you here?


00:45:43.907 --> 00:45:46.147
I don't think your girlfriend
would be too happy if she knew.


00:45:46.179 --> 00:45:48.132
Mmm, never said
she was my girlfriend.


00:45:49.635 --> 00:45:50.916
Why didn't you tell me?


00:45:51.652 --> 00:45:52.932
Tell you what?


00:45:54.052 --> 00:45:55.460
That you're only into...


00:45:55.491 --> 00:45:58.372
Girls?
Never said that either.


00:46:01.123 --> 00:46:02.467
I'm so confused.


00:46:16.547 --> 00:46:18.308
Oi! What the hell
are you doing?


00:46:29.956 --> 00:46:32.228
Hey. Don't tell anyone
about this, yeah?


00:46:32.964 --> 00:46:35.684
Red, if this is about Sikes,
you don't need to be scared.


00:46:35.716 --> 00:46:37.860
It's not me
I'm scared for.


00:46:55.204 --> 00:46:57.284
Got you!


00:46:57.315 --> 00:46:59.876
You think you're clever, don't you?
Call the police, love.


00:46:59.907 --> 00:47:02.244
- I will 'cause you're assaulting him!
- Assaulting him?


00:47:02.275 --> 00:47:05.059
- Yeah!
- This little bellend has been vandalizing property


00:47:05.092 --> 00:47:08.452
of the council with his
shitty little paintings.


00:47:08.483 --> 00:47:10.212
You wanna go as well, eh?


00:47:10.243 --> 00:47:11.523
Come on!


00:47:11.554 --> 00:47:13.667
Here they are.
Get down there, you! Go on.


00:47:13.700 --> 00:47:16.548
She's with the bellend there.
Arrest them.


00:47:16.579 --> 00:47:18.403
- Stay with them. It'll be okay.
- Come on, Son.


00:47:18.852 --> 00:47:20.100
I'll get Fagin.
Go on.


00:47:20.132 --> 00:47:21.828
Thank you.
All right.


00:47:29.764 --> 00:47:31.460
Personally I think
it's an improvement.


00:47:33.251 --> 00:47:34.405
So let me go.


00:47:35.171 --> 00:47:38.147
Unfortunately,
Metropolis Parking Solutions...


00:47:38.178 --> 00:47:40.291
That's the company
whose property you vandalized,


00:47:40.324 --> 00:47:43.109
they don't quite share
the same views.


00:47:48.356 --> 00:47:49.988
Little Ollie Twister.


00:47:55.906 --> 00:47:58.436
Look, to be honest, Oliver,
a little bit of graffiti


00:47:58.468 --> 00:48:00.740
is not really
what concerns me.


00:48:01.155 --> 00:48:03.171
You kind of running
into Warden Bumble,


00:48:03.204 --> 00:48:04.996
well that's just kind
of fortuitous for me.


00:48:05.028 --> 00:48:06.404
It's like
a happy accident.


00:48:07.139 --> 00:48:09.380
What I really wanna talk
to you about is...


00:48:12.995 --> 00:48:14.564
this man.


00:48:15.939 --> 00:48:16.964
Fagin.


00:48:17.794 --> 00:48:19.747
An alias, obviously.


00:48:19.779 --> 00:48:22.307
A once prestigious
art dealer.


00:48:22.339 --> 00:48:24.068
Then out of the blue...


00:48:24.099 --> 00:48:25.732
...vanishes.
Disappears.


00:48:26.403 --> 00:48:29.091
And since then, it seems
like he's been putting


00:48:29.124 --> 00:48:31.813
his knowledge of art
to more practical usage.


00:48:32.324 --> 00:48:35.045
Apparently he's running
quite the operation.


00:48:37.316 --> 00:48:38.629
Yeah.


00:48:39.715 --> 00:48:41.379
And what about
this lovely lady?


00:48:41.411 --> 00:48:42.916
Known associate of Fagin.


00:48:42.946 --> 00:48:44.292
Sikes.


00:48:45.763 --> 00:48:47.492
How am I supposed
to know these two?


00:48:49.314 --> 00:48:50.947
How am I supposed to...


00:48:52.547 --> 00:48:55.012
Nancy Lee, alias Red.


00:48:55.043 --> 00:48:57.955
Known associate of
both Sikes and Fagin's.


00:49:01.251 --> 00:49:02.947
It's a pretty girl,
Oliver.


00:49:08.931 --> 00:49:10.531
I can get you out of this,
you know.


00:49:11.299 --> 00:49:14.051
- Get me out of what?
- Ah, see, now that,


00:49:14.082 --> 00:49:16.387
that's exactly what I'm
hoping you're gonna tell me.


00:49:16.420 --> 00:49:18.052
Because your little friends,
your new pals,


00:49:18.084 --> 00:49:20.773
they're not all
that they seem.


00:49:21.252 --> 00:49:23.652
And to be perfectly honest,
friends of Fagin and Sikes


00:49:23.683 --> 00:49:25.572
have a nasty habit
of ending up, well...


00:49:29.059 --> 00:49:30.628
like that.


00:49:30.658 --> 00:49:32.931
Tom Chitling.
He died last month.


00:49:32.964 --> 00:49:35.332
Take a good look, Oliver.


00:49:35.363 --> 00:49:36.612
I don't even know this Sikes.


00:49:37.667 --> 00:49:39.332
Are you sure?


00:49:40.484 --> 00:49:41.989
I'm sure.


00:49:44.003 --> 00:49:45.029
Okay.


00:49:45.635 --> 00:49:47.715
Well,
you're free to go.


00:49:48.738 --> 00:49:52.003
Just be careful who you trust because
people only see what they wanna see.


00:49:54.467 --> 00:49:55.651
Off you go, then.


00:50:04.611 --> 00:50:05.956
You're late.


00:50:07.299 --> 00:50:08.803
Where's Twist?


00:50:09.891 --> 00:50:11.140
He was with you,
right, Dodge?


00:50:16.196 --> 00:50:18.596
Just wanted to get a run-in.
I lost track of time.


00:50:19.554 --> 00:50:20.868
I don't know
where Twist is.


00:50:20.899 --> 00:50:22.819
I gave them all the night off.


00:50:22.850 --> 00:50:25.571
Those paintings are going
nowhere till the morning.


00:50:25.604 --> 00:50:27.299
It is morning.
Where is he?


00:50:40.964 --> 00:50:42.756
- Who is this?
- <i>Think of me</i>


00:50:42.787 --> 00:50:44.803
<i>as the friendly uncle
you never had.</i>


00:50:44.835 --> 00:50:47.139
<i>I just wanted to make sure
you've got my number.</i>


00:50:47.780 --> 00:50:50.340
<i>In case you remember anything
about our Ms. Sikes.</i>


00:50:50.372 --> 00:50:51.621
I won't.


00:50:52.356 --> 00:50:54.500
You got some explaining
to do, boy.


00:50:56.355 --> 00:50:59.139
- Where you been, then?
- I went to a pub with Dodge and Batesy.


00:50:59.170 --> 00:51:01.603
They got back hours ago.
What happened to you?


00:51:02.595 --> 00:51:05.763
- I got arrested.
- Been having little words, have we?


00:51:05.795 --> 00:51:07.044
No, it wasn't
like that.


00:51:07.076 --> 00:51:08.708
It was this traffic warden.


00:51:08.739 --> 00:51:10.372
I wrote on his van
and he wasn't happy about it.


00:51:10.402 --> 00:51:12.196
You wrote
on his van last night?


00:51:12.227 --> 00:51:13.763
No, last week.


00:51:13.796 --> 00:51:15.459
I bumped into him
this morning...


00:51:15.491 --> 00:51:17.092
How come
the cops let you go?


00:51:17.891 --> 00:51:19.811
Did you give them
something they wanted?


00:51:19.843 --> 00:51:21.700
No, nothing.
I gave them nothing.


00:51:21.732 --> 00:51:23.108
If he grassed,
why would he come back here?


00:51:23.139 --> 00:51:24.292
Was I talking to you?


00:51:24.324 --> 00:51:26.180
- I'm just saying, I...
- Don't!


00:51:26.211 --> 00:51:28.483
- We need him.
- <i>Hello, Artnet.</i>


00:51:28.515 --> 00:51:30.595
- <i>Hello, it's Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>
- Shh!


00:51:30.628 --> 00:51:32.643
<i>My vault is flooded, so I need
to move a painting to Dotheboy's.</i>


00:51:32.674 --> 00:51:34.371
He's on the phone
with the couriers.


00:51:34.402 --> 00:51:35.748
They're arranging a pickup.


00:51:35.779 --> 00:51:37.219
<i>One second.</i>


00:51:38.531 --> 00:51:40.195
Round three.


00:51:41.378 --> 00:51:43.107
The painting is gonna be
on the move.


00:51:43.138 --> 00:51:44.867
This is it.


00:51:44.898 --> 00:51:47.075
You better pray this time
it goes like clockwork.


00:51:49.732 --> 00:51:52.100
Remember,
I'm watching.


00:52:00.804 --> 00:52:02.948
I'm claustrophobic,
okay.


00:52:02.979 --> 00:52:05.412
Nobody told me that
it was gonna be that small.


00:52:05.827 --> 00:52:08.388
- Quit making a fuss and get in.
- I'm not making a fuss.


00:52:08.420 --> 00:52:11.138
I'm claustrophobic.
It's an actual condition.


00:52:11.171 --> 00:52:13.667
If Batesy gets in there
and passes out,


00:52:13.699 --> 00:52:15.556
the whole plan's screwed.
What are we gonna do?


00:52:15.587 --> 00:52:17.572
Exactly. And there is
every chance


00:52:17.603 --> 00:52:19.652
that if I get in there
I will pass out.


00:52:19.683 --> 00:52:21.476
Batesy,
don't be such a baby.


00:52:21.507 --> 00:52:23.523
What are you gonna do?
Force him down?


00:52:23.555 --> 00:52:25.635
You say you're gonna do
something then don't do it.


00:52:25.666 --> 00:52:28.964
Are we gonna do this,
or you gonna stand there arguing all day?


00:52:28.995 --> 00:52:30.084
Well, he's in now.


00:52:31.234 --> 00:52:34.372
All right. Anybody tries
to moves the crate,


00:52:34.404 --> 00:52:36.900
you set off the smoke bomb
in their face.


00:52:37.731 --> 00:52:38.915
Piece of cake.


00:52:39.586 --> 00:52:41.027
All right. That's it.


00:52:43.331 --> 00:52:44.323
Let's do it then.


00:52:47.618 --> 00:52:48.708
Really?


00:53:00.355 --> 00:53:02.563
Delivery to our gallery
in W1, yeah?


00:53:02.595 --> 00:53:03.875
Yeah, copy that, darling.


00:53:03.908 --> 00:53:05.348
We just got
a few drop-offs first.


00:53:05.380 --> 00:53:06.532
Cheers, lads.


00:53:30.435 --> 00:53:32.963
I thought we were only sharing travel
with the National Gallery piece.


00:53:32.995 --> 00:53:34.531
Uh, let me see.


00:53:34.562 --> 00:53:36.196
Originally yours
was dropped off first


00:53:36.227 --> 00:53:37.572
and then on
to the National Gallery.


00:53:37.603 --> 00:53:39.268
It's just an extra
pickup, mate.


00:53:39.298 --> 00:53:40.644
It won't affect
your drop-off time.


00:53:40.674 --> 00:53:43.042
They're close together,
you see.


00:53:43.074 --> 00:53:46.915
- Chiswell Fine Arts.
- I've never heard of it.


00:53:53.507 --> 00:53:55.907
You ever heard of
a Chiswell Fine Arts, Rosie?


00:53:55.939 --> 00:53:57.475
Somewhere near here?


00:53:57.890 --> 00:54:00.099
I thought you knew all
the galleries in London.


00:54:02.979 --> 00:54:04.963
I'll google it.


00:54:10.882 --> 00:54:13.284
Can't find a Chiswell.


00:54:16.003 --> 00:54:17.763
Get me Artnet
on the phone now!


00:54:39.011 --> 00:54:40.676
What's all this?


00:54:47.298 --> 00:54:48.579
You all right?
What's occurring?


00:54:48.610 --> 00:54:50.468
- Can we get through?
- How you doing?


00:54:50.498 --> 00:54:51.908
- Yeah, fine.
- Where you from?


00:54:51.939 --> 00:54:53.475
- I'm from Fullham.
- Fullham?


00:54:53.506 --> 00:54:56.291
I've got cousins in Fullham.
You know Phil?


00:54:56.323 --> 00:54:58.243
- No.
- You must know my second cousin.


00:54:58.275 --> 00:55:00.035
- What's her name? Oh, Tracey.
- No.


00:55:00.067 --> 00:55:01.859
- Can we get through?
- Can you get through?


00:55:01.891 --> 00:55:04.003
I don't know...


00:55:04.035 --> 00:55:06.596
<i>7-4, receiving. 7-4, receiving.</i>


00:55:06.626 --> 00:55:08.452
Is there aliens?
I mean...


00:55:08.482 --> 00:55:09.891
7-4. Go ahead.


00:55:09.923 --> 00:55:12.067
<i>Just had a call from
the Losberne Gallery.</i>


00:55:12.100 --> 00:55:14.339
<i>They seem to think
they're being robbed.</i>


00:55:14.371 --> 00:55:17.315
Is it real?
Is life even real?


00:55:17.347 --> 00:55:18.787
Everything all right,
lads?


00:55:19.875 --> 00:55:21.411
Floor it!


00:55:35.618 --> 00:55:37.219
No!


00:55:38.724 --> 00:55:40.867
Sikes, no.
No, Sikes!


00:55:41.411 --> 00:55:42.916
Please, Sikes.


00:55:45.891 --> 00:55:47.011
Run!


00:55:47.972 --> 00:55:50.819
- Where is it? Give it to me.
- I didn't get it. I'm sorry.


00:55:50.851 --> 00:55:53.891
We need a distraction.
Move. Move!


00:55:58.594 --> 00:56:00.642
When I said "don't,"
that means don't go this way.


00:56:00.675 --> 00:56:03.011
- <i>...female in a red leather jacket.</i>
- Hey!


00:56:03.042 --> 00:56:05.026
Female suspect heading west
down Pass Road.


00:56:05.059 --> 00:56:07.427
<i>Officers are in pursuit.
Officers are in pursuit.</i>


00:56:20.260 --> 00:56:21.828
I'm asking you
very nicely to stop.


00:56:25.475 --> 00:56:26.724
There it is.


00:56:51.138 --> 00:56:53.060
I really need
to start going to the gym.


00:56:53.955 --> 00:56:55.075
This is...


00:57:05.699 --> 00:57:06.948
Uh...


00:57:08.642 --> 00:57:10.370
<i>Bedwin, give me an update.</i>


00:57:10.402 --> 00:57:12.611
Brownlow, we got some good news
and some bad news.


00:57:12.643 --> 00:57:15.106
- <i>Fill me in then.</i>
- Yeah, well, the bad news is I haven't got her.


00:57:15.234 --> 00:57:18.275
- <i>What's the good news?</i>
- There is no good news, really, if I'm honest.


00:57:18.307 --> 00:57:20.003
<i>Get yourself back here now.</i>


00:57:26.947 --> 00:57:28.483
Oi! Get in.


00:57:29.284 --> 00:57:31.523
- I need to work on my cardio.
- How come Twist was


00:57:31.555 --> 00:57:33.284
in the back of that van?
Should have been you.


00:57:34.179 --> 00:57:37.443
Well, I'm claustrophobic,
so we just switched places.


00:57:39.940 --> 00:57:41.284
You shouldn't have.


00:57:48.227 --> 00:57:49.764
Batesy!


00:58:25.346 --> 00:58:27.074
He should have been
back by now.


00:58:27.106 --> 00:58:29.059
Quiet. I'm trying to think.


00:58:29.508 --> 00:58:31.715
That was our one shot.


00:58:33.154 --> 00:58:35.106
It was bad luck
is all.


00:58:35.555 --> 00:58:37.059
Bad luck? There's no such thing.


00:58:37.091 --> 00:58:39.747
It was a simple plan
until that bloody Twist


00:58:39.779 --> 00:58:41.954
decided to go in the van.


00:58:48.194 --> 00:58:50.052
Mate, have you seen...


00:58:52.323 --> 00:58:53.891
What happened
to Tom Chitling?


00:58:53.923 --> 00:58:55.011
He fell.


00:58:56.770 --> 00:59:00.610
- Did you see it?
- Someone has been misinforming you, Oliver.


00:59:00.643 --> 00:59:05.059
- Don't avoid the question!
- I just don't think it's you asking the questions.


00:59:05.091 --> 00:59:07.012
Who have you been talking to?


00:59:09.667 --> 00:59:11.172
Sikes.


00:59:11.778 --> 00:59:13.987
Why don't you ask her?


00:59:15.107 --> 00:59:16.899
- Sikes!
- He's a rat!


00:59:17.379 --> 00:59:19.427
Van suddenly peels off.
They knew what was going down.


00:59:19.459 --> 00:59:20.868
- I didn't tell them anything!
- Lies!


00:59:22.915 --> 00:59:24.259
What's this, eh?


00:59:26.883 --> 00:59:28.707
Thing I need to know, Twist,


00:59:28.739 --> 00:59:30.467
is how you hold up
under a beating.


00:59:31.011 --> 00:59:32.354
I bet you fall
to pieces, eh?


00:59:32.387 --> 00:59:33.603
Fagin, make her stop.


00:59:42.146 --> 00:59:43.874
Question is,
do you want some more?


00:59:46.659 --> 00:59:47.780
Hold him.


00:59:49.123 --> 00:59:51.202
Sikes, don't make it
permanent.


00:59:51.234 --> 00:59:52.963
Right, Bullseye,
on my command.


00:59:54.402 --> 00:59:56.354
You're making a mistake.


00:59:56.834 --> 00:59:58.243
A mistake?


00:59:59.106 --> 01:00:01.028
He got in trouble
with the traffic warden.


01:00:01.059 --> 01:00:02.916
And how would
you know that, Red?


01:00:03.554 --> 01:00:04.932
'Cause I was there.


01:00:06.050 --> 01:00:07.171
What?


01:00:09.411 --> 01:00:11.267
We were on our way home
and the traffic warden


01:00:11.299 --> 01:00:13.123
came out of nowhere
and tackled him to the ground.


01:00:13.155 --> 01:00:15.107
- Just like he said.
- On your way home from where?


01:00:17.698 --> 01:00:18.787
We...


01:00:20.003 --> 01:00:21.860
We went for a swim together.


01:00:34.851 --> 01:00:36.675
If he moves, shoot him.


01:00:36.707 --> 01:00:38.755
Come with me.


01:00:38.786 --> 01:00:40.003
Bullseye, stay.


01:00:52.675 --> 01:00:54.371
This ain't like Batesy.


01:00:54.402 --> 01:00:56.386
He gets withdrawal symptoms
if he ain't plugged in.


01:00:56.419 --> 01:00:58.723
- Batesy's dead.
- What?


01:00:58.754 --> 01:01:00.035
Just like she killed Tom.


01:01:00.610 --> 01:01:02.690
- But Sikes said...
- Tom was murdered!


01:01:03.426 --> 01:01:05.570
He didn't go off
that roof by accident.


01:01:06.851 --> 01:01:08.259
How would you know that?


01:01:09.411 --> 01:01:10.660
I got a text
off that phone.


01:01:12.226 --> 01:01:13.762
Some cop gave it to me
to see if I'd turn.


01:01:13.795 --> 01:01:15.523
And did you turn?


01:01:15.555 --> 01:01:18.500
Or were you never
with this family to begin with?


01:01:19.010 --> 01:01:20.675
You call this a family?


01:01:21.379 --> 01:01:22.946
When that psycho is
out there with Red


01:01:22.979 --> 01:01:24.579
and you're pointing
a gun at me!


01:01:25.731 --> 01:01:26.947
I don't believe you.


01:01:26.978 --> 01:01:28.514
I'm gonna go find Batesy myself.


01:01:28.547 --> 01:01:30.052
You're gonna be looking
six feet under.


01:01:30.499 --> 01:01:33.283
He's right. I pushed Tom.


01:01:33.314 --> 01:01:35.170
- You lying piece...
- Please.


01:01:35.202 --> 01:01:36.995
Give me an excuse to kill you.


01:01:37.411 --> 01:01:38.627
You can't kill all of us.


01:01:39.394 --> 01:01:40.579
Let's see, shall we?


01:01:41.155 --> 01:01:43.363
Six bullets, three kids.
You do the math.


01:01:43.395 --> 01:01:45.731
We're hitting Dotheboy's.
We're getting that painting.


01:01:45.763 --> 01:01:47.619
Dotheboy's?
I think the whole plan


01:01:47.650 --> 01:01:50.146
was to get the painting
before it went there.


01:01:50.178 --> 01:01:52.387
That place
is impenetrable.


01:01:52.419 --> 01:01:54.019
You scared, old man?


01:01:54.530 --> 01:01:56.931
I'll have a plan
in four hours.


01:01:57.442 --> 01:02:00.483
Try not to kill any more
of them in the meantime.


01:02:03.138 --> 01:02:04.451
I can't promise anything.


01:02:12.898 --> 01:02:15.010
<i>Look, mate,
I believe ya.</i>


01:02:15.683 --> 01:02:18.019
<i>What Sikes did to Tom,
that's messed up.</i>


01:02:18.594 --> 01:02:20.899
But if we don't do this,
we'll lose Red too.


01:02:22.403 --> 01:02:24.163
Sikes is a loose cannon.


01:02:24.194 --> 01:02:26.243
Let's just suck it up
and get on with it, yeah?


01:02:27.938 --> 01:02:29.283
Let's do this.


01:02:35.970 --> 01:02:37.058
<i>Is he on time?</i>


01:02:37.090 --> 01:02:39.780
Like clockwork. We're on.


01:02:52.227 --> 01:02:53.891
Can I get two sugars
with that, as well?


01:02:54.626 --> 01:02:56.354
All right there, mates?
Sorry to interrupt.


01:02:56.386 --> 01:02:58.210
Can I get a Bakewell tart,
please?


01:02:58.242 --> 01:02:59.747
Sure.


01:03:00.259 --> 01:03:02.083
- It's chippy, innit?
- Yeah, I know. It's freezing.


01:03:02.115 --> 01:03:03.843
There you go. 1.50.


01:03:04.292 --> 01:03:05.634
There you go.
Keep the change.


01:03:06.882 --> 01:03:07.972
Thanks.


01:03:10.211 --> 01:03:11.522
Have a good day,
lads.


01:03:11.554 --> 01:03:12.739
See ya.


01:03:27.074 --> 01:03:30.530
<i>The painting will be under
lock and key before the auction.</i>


01:03:30.946 --> 01:03:33.891
<i>So our only chance is
during the main event.</i>


01:03:33.922 --> 01:03:36.610
<i>We'll go in at the front
and at the right moment</i>


01:03:36.643 --> 01:03:39.523
<i>execute the plan,
sending the painting your way.</i>


01:03:39.554 --> 01:03:41.571
Let's play happy families, eh?
Big smiles.


01:03:59.459 --> 01:04:01.123
Thank you.


01:04:01.154 --> 01:04:03.074
Whoa, whoa.


01:04:03.106 --> 01:04:05.123
It's the chair. Really?


01:04:05.635 --> 01:04:06.819
Jesus.


01:04:23.426 --> 01:04:25.442
There you go.


01:04:25.474 --> 01:04:28.099
<i>Dodge, once you're
inside, let Twist in.</i>


01:04:28.131 --> 01:04:30.210
<i>Then, when all hell
has broken loose,</i>


01:04:30.242 --> 01:04:31.362
<i>you know what to do.</i>


01:04:36.803 --> 01:04:38.051
Gang's all here.


01:04:46.530 --> 01:04:48.323
Don't do anything stupid.


01:04:57.283 --> 01:05:00.130
I'm glad you're finally taking
this threat seriously, Officer.


01:05:01.794 --> 01:05:03.396
Detective Inspector.


01:05:09.762 --> 01:05:11.172
How many men
have you deployed?


01:05:12.291 --> 01:05:13.635
There's 12
inside the building.


01:05:14.466 --> 01:05:16.163
Another 20 outside.


01:05:19.810 --> 01:05:21.315
Nobody is getting
this painting, Losberne.


01:05:21.346 --> 01:05:22.979
Doctor Losberne.


01:05:32.962 --> 01:05:34.594
Better you than me,
mate.


01:05:50.818 --> 01:05:52.387
<i>Lot 146.</i>


01:05:53.123 --> 01:05:54.914
William Hogarth's painting


01:05:54.946 --> 01:05:57.635
<i>A Harlot's Progress,
The Arrest.</i>


01:05:57.666 --> 01:06:00.546
Oil on canvas. 1731.


01:06:00.578 --> 01:06:02.658
Has resurfaced
after many years,


01:06:02.690 --> 01:06:05.442
as the only surviving <i>Harlot's
Progress</i> from the fire...


01:06:05.474 --> 01:06:06.979
Now.


01:06:07.555 --> 01:06:11.139
We start the reserve
price of three million pounds.


01:06:11.169 --> 01:06:12.642
Yes, madam.


01:06:14.018 --> 01:06:16.770
And you, sir? At the back there, sir? Yes.


01:06:16.803 --> 01:06:18.403
Three million two.


01:06:18.435 --> 01:06:19.971
I have three million,
200 thousand pounds.


01:06:22.241 --> 01:06:23.747
He's got a gun!


01:06:25.699 --> 01:06:27.619
- Stay calm.
- It was a trap.


01:06:27.649 --> 01:06:30.338
- They're after my painting!
- Get it back in the vault!


01:06:30.370 --> 01:06:32.035
It'll be safe.
It's the safest place.


01:06:37.315 --> 01:06:39.714
- Over there, look.
- Through that door.


01:06:44.482 --> 01:06:47.203
There's a robbery in progress.
Stay with the painting.


01:06:47.235 --> 01:06:49.091
Get it to the vault.
Let's go! Let's move.


01:06:52.322 --> 01:06:54.242
Wait, wait, wait.


01:06:54.274 --> 01:06:55.939
I'm coming with you.


01:06:55.970 --> 01:06:57.283
No one goes
down there but us.


01:06:57.314 --> 01:06:59.075
There's a robbery in progress.


01:06:59.107 --> 01:07:01.986
- Yeah, we have our procedures.
- And I have my orders.


01:07:02.019 --> 01:07:04.771
And that painting ain't going
anywhere without me.


01:07:04.803 --> 01:07:06.755
What... What's going on?


01:07:06.786 --> 01:07:09.571
- Who are you?
- Officer Dawkins, Sergeant.


01:07:09.602 --> 01:07:11.362
- Dawkins? Good.
- Yeah.


01:07:53.123 --> 01:07:55.907
Okay. You guys go that way.
You guys come with me. Let's go.


01:08:02.146 --> 01:08:03.330
You.


01:08:04.002 --> 01:08:06.371
Yes, it's me.


01:08:08.001 --> 01:08:09.954
Ah, that felt good.


01:08:25.570 --> 01:08:27.619
Good. This is good.
This is very good.


01:08:28.642 --> 01:08:30.148
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


01:08:33.410 --> 01:08:34.596
Show me the painting.


01:08:36.193 --> 01:08:37.186
Ah...


01:08:39.042 --> 01:08:40.898
I'll be honest,
not his best work.


01:08:44.738 --> 01:08:46.147
Move!


01:08:46.178 --> 01:08:47.171
Okay.


01:08:51.266 --> 01:08:53.090
Oh, you silly sausage.


01:08:53.122 --> 01:08:54.403
You're going nowhere, Son.


01:08:56.257 --> 01:08:57.763
Shit!


01:08:59.715 --> 01:09:01.730
Brownlow,
you're wrong about Twist.


01:09:01.762 --> 01:09:03.203
He's in the lift shaft.


01:09:03.234 --> 01:09:04.962
Yeah, the dirty swine.


01:09:06.466 --> 01:09:07.940
Well, move then.


01:09:11.618 --> 01:09:13.634
I'm coming for you, Twist.


01:09:13.665 --> 01:09:16.579
- No, no, no!
- If you think a lift is gonna stop me...


01:09:17.475 --> 01:09:20.291
- Oh, you got nowhere to hide, boy.
- Dodge!


01:09:20.323 --> 01:09:21.379
- You muppet.
- Dodge?


01:09:21.410 --> 01:09:23.234
You...


01:09:23.265 --> 01:09:24.322
Hurry up.


01:09:24.354 --> 01:09:25.538
- Dodge.
- Come on.


01:09:25.570 --> 01:09:26.818
Help me!


01:09:26.851 --> 01:09:28.739
- Hurry up.
- Help!


01:09:28.770 --> 01:09:30.755
- Come on.
- I'm coming!


01:09:30.787 --> 01:09:32.419
Get these bloody doors open!


01:09:41.858 --> 01:09:43.107
Hurry up, Dodge!


01:09:56.641 --> 01:09:58.146
Oi!


01:10:04.545 --> 01:10:06.081
Wait a minute.


01:10:06.113 --> 01:10:08.066
Give me a break.
You're not thinking we...


01:10:08.098 --> 01:10:10.275
- Oi! Stop!
- Come on!


01:10:12.898 --> 01:10:15.459
- Ready? Belt.
- Twist, what are you doing? This is madness.


01:10:15.489 --> 01:10:17.058
Three, two, one...


01:10:20.354 --> 01:10:21.538
Hang on!


01:10:22.338 --> 01:10:23.843
Wait, wait...


01:10:23.874 --> 01:10:25.058
Let go!


01:10:31.010 --> 01:10:32.802
Okay.


01:10:32.834 --> 01:10:34.082
Congratulations.


01:10:35.107 --> 01:10:36.227
All the best.


01:10:39.938 --> 01:10:41.827
Brownlow, you need
to get down here right now.


01:10:47.265 --> 01:10:48.514
Shit!


01:10:48.546 --> 01:10:51.906
Shit, shit!


01:10:51.938 --> 01:10:54.018
- Flippin' hell.
- Let's go up here.


01:10:55.937 --> 01:10:57.699
I think we've lost them.


01:10:57.729 --> 01:10:59.779
They wouldn't have got far,
Losberne.


01:10:59.810 --> 01:11:01.154
Well,
you better be right.


01:11:01.794 --> 01:11:03.586
- Come on. Let's go.
- Hey! Hey!


01:11:03.617 --> 01:11:05.123
Don't even think about it!
Do not move.


01:11:05.153 --> 01:11:07.425
Hello?


01:11:07.457 --> 01:11:09.506
- <i>Your delivery's here.</i>
- I didn't order anything.


01:11:10.243 --> 01:11:12.643
- Hey, don't!
- Dodge, let's go!


01:11:13.634 --> 01:11:15.106
Hey!


01:11:15.138 --> 01:11:17.155
Get after them!
Don't leave, hey!


01:11:17.185 --> 01:11:19.235
- Come back here! Come...
- Wait!


01:11:19.266 --> 01:11:22.274
Get them... Hey, stop!


01:11:22.305 --> 01:11:24.866
Stop! Make him stop!


01:11:42.307 --> 01:11:45.091
There's only one person
who could do this.


01:11:51.170 --> 01:11:52.706
<i>Batesy.</i>


01:11:52.737 --> 01:11:54.050
Enjoy your munch, did ya?


01:11:54.082 --> 01:11:56.578
You magnificent bastard.


01:11:56.611 --> 01:12:00.482
You had us worried sick, mate.
Where are ya?


01:12:00.513 --> 01:12:03.330
You know Sikes has gone
full-blown psycho, don't you?


01:12:03.362 --> 01:12:05.025
- <i>She tried to kill me.</i>
- What?


01:12:05.058 --> 01:12:06.531
We're on our way
to see her now.


01:12:06.562 --> 01:12:08.386
<i>No, don't! It ain't safe.</i>


01:12:08.418 --> 01:12:10.915
What do you mean?
We got no choice.


01:12:10.946 --> 01:12:13.091
<i>Red's with her.
We're all heading to Fagin's.</i>


01:12:14.243 --> 01:12:15.875
All right, well,
I'll meet you there.


01:12:15.907 --> 01:12:17.411
- <i>Just look after yourself.</i>
- Okay.


01:12:18.593 --> 01:12:20.642
That was Batesy. He's...


01:12:23.234 --> 01:12:24.418
Twist?


01:12:28.898 --> 01:12:30.114
Twist?


01:12:33.857 --> 01:12:35.683
You're late.
Where is he?


01:12:36.257 --> 01:12:37.986
I don't know.
We got split up.


01:12:38.017 --> 01:12:39.585
- Who's got it?
- He has.


01:12:39.618 --> 01:12:40.835
Oi!


01:12:41.762 --> 01:12:43.906
- You miss me?
- Bates.


01:12:44.482 --> 01:12:46.306
You all right?
What happened?


01:12:46.337 --> 01:12:48.451
Thought I dealt with you,
fuck's sake.


01:12:48.481 --> 01:12:50.561
- Where's Twist?
- I'm right here.


01:12:58.402 --> 01:13:00.258
You want the painting?
She's coming with me.


01:13:01.539 --> 01:13:02.979
Do you think she's worth it?


01:13:06.721 --> 01:13:07.714
Try me.


01:13:09.250 --> 01:13:10.851
Do what he says.


01:13:15.458 --> 01:13:17.539
You got more stones than
I gave you credit for.


01:13:19.329 --> 01:13:20.835
Give me that.


01:13:26.689 --> 01:13:28.642
I'll always be
a step ahead of you.


01:13:32.033 --> 01:13:33.890
You think
you can just take my girl?


01:13:35.265 --> 01:13:36.290
It's the painting, Sikes.


01:13:36.737 --> 01:13:38.946
Give me the envelope
and let him go.


01:13:40.034 --> 01:13:41.154
You sure that's it, Fagin?


01:13:46.050 --> 01:13:47.971
- What?
- The painting.


01:13:48.641 --> 01:13:50.018
Are you sure
it's the right one?


01:13:54.722 --> 01:13:56.611
Easy. Easy.


01:13:57.185 --> 01:13:58.850
I'm just reaching for my phone.


01:13:59.425 --> 01:14:01.346
You guys might wanna see this.


01:14:07.298 --> 01:14:09.155
You see,
before I got into graffiti,


01:14:09.922 --> 01:14:11.587
I used to paint.


01:14:11.618 --> 01:14:14.881
You lot mentioning Hogarth
got me inspired.


01:14:14.914 --> 01:14:16.739
It's not bad, eh, Fagin?


01:14:17.505 --> 01:14:18.690
Where is it?


01:14:19.073 --> 01:14:20.771
I walk out of here
with Red.


01:14:21.505 --> 01:14:23.298
I'll call you
and tell you where it is.


01:14:23.329 --> 01:14:24.675
She stays with me.


01:14:26.081 --> 01:14:27.682
We need the painting, Sikes.


01:14:27.713 --> 01:14:29.570
Whose side are you on?


01:14:29.602 --> 01:14:32.707
All this has got to stop.
You're done. We're done.


01:14:32.739 --> 01:14:34.723
All bets are off.


01:14:34.754 --> 01:14:37.826
Get me the envelope
and I'll let you leave.


01:14:51.298 --> 01:14:52.481
Come on.


01:14:53.378 --> 01:14:54.913
You'll let me leave?


01:15:01.154 --> 01:15:02.850
I choose how this ends.


01:15:03.873 --> 01:15:05.507
- Fagin, Fagin.
- Fagin.


01:15:06.018 --> 01:15:07.011
Fagin?


01:15:13.090 --> 01:15:14.466
Come on!


01:15:15.202 --> 01:15:17.346
Quick! Come on, Twist!


01:15:29.857 --> 01:15:31.266
Come on!


01:15:35.778 --> 01:15:37.219
You go first.


01:15:37.250 --> 01:15:38.691
I'm not going without you!


01:15:38.722 --> 01:15:40.963
Listen, jump.
I'll be right behind you.


01:15:41.473 --> 01:15:42.466
Go.


01:15:59.553 --> 01:16:01.345
Twist! Twist.


01:16:01.377 --> 01:16:02.626
Hold on, hold on.


01:16:02.657 --> 01:16:04.227
Come on!


01:16:08.994 --> 01:16:11.298
Twist! Come on.


01:16:11.330 --> 01:16:12.674
Don't let go.


01:16:20.289 --> 01:16:22.274
No! No!


01:16:25.219 --> 01:16:28.355
- Pull him up, Sikes.
- I'm sure he'll be fine. Step back!


01:16:28.385 --> 01:16:30.465
Look at him, not even strong
enough to pull himself up.


01:16:30.498 --> 01:16:33.026
- He's so weak.
- He's not weak!


01:16:33.058 --> 01:16:35.842
- You need to come with me now.
- I don't need you anymore.


01:16:35.873 --> 01:16:37.602
You think Twist is
the one for you?


01:16:37.633 --> 01:16:39.011
He's more than
you will ever be.


01:16:39.041 --> 01:16:40.739
I dragged you from the gutter,
looked after you,


01:16:40.770 --> 01:16:42.530
gave you everything
you needed.


01:16:42.561 --> 01:16:43.810
Sikes!


01:17:00.610 --> 01:17:03.843
What a fine thing
capital punishment is.


01:17:36.578 --> 01:17:38.051
Young man.


01:17:41.281 --> 01:17:43.202
I'm guessing you heard
about the reward?


01:17:47.265 --> 01:17:48.867
Be there in five.


01:17:53.889 --> 01:17:56.289
Do we know what we're meant
to be waiting for?


01:17:56.321 --> 01:17:58.499
We don't have a clue,
Bedwin.


01:17:58.529 --> 01:18:00.515
I'm sure we'll know
when we see it.


01:18:00.546 --> 01:18:02.691
He's not exactly just gonna stroll in.


01:18:02.721 --> 01:18:05.250
- He's literally just strolled in.
- All right, lads?


01:18:05.761 --> 01:18:08.161
- You hungry?
- You got a lot of nerve showing up.


01:18:08.193 --> 01:18:10.306
- Let's just nick him now.
- Calm down, Bedwin.


01:18:10.338 --> 01:18:12.002
You look like you could do
with a bacon sarnie.


01:18:12.034 --> 01:18:13.762
This might be funny to you,
but this is serious.


01:18:13.792 --> 01:18:15.009
I need your full cooperation.


01:18:15.042 --> 01:18:17.059
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Cooperation?


01:18:17.666 --> 01:18:19.235
I've done you guys a favor.


01:18:20.001 --> 01:18:21.634
How's that?


01:18:21.666 --> 01:18:22.754
Where's the painting?


01:18:22.784 --> 01:18:24.067
I don't have it.


01:18:24.098 --> 01:18:25.602
So where is it?


01:18:25.634 --> 01:18:27.361
I'm not the criminal here.
In fact,


01:18:27.394 --> 01:18:28.898
I've done all the work
for you guys.


01:18:28.929 --> 01:18:30.786
Two bacon sarnies.


01:18:30.817 --> 01:18:32.066
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


01:18:32.097 --> 01:18:33.730
Excuse me. I didn't order this.


01:18:33.762 --> 01:18:36.035
Oh, no, it's fine.
It's my treat.


01:18:36.065 --> 01:18:38.177
Well, that's very kind of you,
young man.


01:18:38.210 --> 01:18:41.378
- Yes, very kind.
- But don't think this is getting you out of trouble.


01:18:41.409 --> 01:18:42.722
I need you to understand
one thing.


01:18:42.753 --> 01:18:44.513
You're gonna need
to start cooperating.


01:18:47.809 --> 01:18:49.217
Oh, brilliant.


01:18:59.330 --> 01:19:01.282
Yeah, hello?
Very smart that was.


01:19:01.313 --> 01:19:02.977
<i>A wise cop
once said to me,</i>


01:19:03.008 --> 01:19:04.929
<i>"People only see
what they wanna see."</i>


01:19:04.961 --> 01:19:07.777
<i>You'll be wanting some
brown sauce with those I assume.</i>


01:19:07.808 --> 01:19:10.466
What do you mean... Hello? Hello?


01:19:13.217 --> 01:19:14.529
Brown sauce.


01:19:17.633 --> 01:19:18.913
Nah, it's...


01:19:22.433 --> 01:19:23.969
It's above
the brown sauce, Bedwin.


01:19:24.001 --> 01:19:25.507
It's above
the brown sauce.


01:19:27.553 --> 01:19:29.090
Holy shit.


01:19:43.297 --> 01:19:46.818
<i>The tale of the stolen Hogarth
in an audacious raid</i>


01:19:46.850 --> 01:19:48.802
<i>took a bizarre twist today</i>


01:19:48.832 --> 01:19:52.130
<i>when a tip-off led detectives
to a lockup in East London</i>


01:19:52.162 --> 01:19:55.970
<i>in which a large collection of
stolen artworks has been discovered.</i>


01:19:56.002 --> 01:20:00.131
<i>The lockup belongs to the art
dealer Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>


01:20:00.705 --> 01:20:04.386
<i>Documents were also found
proving that Dr. Crispin Losberne</i>


01:20:04.417 --> 01:20:07.330
<i>is not the legal owner
of the Hogarth.</i>


01:20:07.362 --> 01:20:10.306
<i>It's alleged that
the well-established art dealer</i>


01:20:10.338 --> 01:20:13.859
<i>has been making his fortune
out of selling stolen artwork</i>


01:20:13.890 --> 01:20:16.482
<i>and faking
the ownership documentation.</i>


01:20:16.514 --> 01:20:19.906
<i>A Mr. Isaac Solomon
has been named as an accomplice.</i>


01:20:19.937 --> 01:20:23.459
<i>It's believed that this man
also goes by the name of Fagin.</i>


01:20:24.065 --> 01:20:26.658
<i>Fagin and Sikes really
had raised some good thieves.</i>


01:20:26.689 --> 01:20:29.505
<i>So good they didn't know
when they were the target.</i>


01:20:34.338 --> 01:20:36.866
<i>The envelope revealed
the true owners of the Hogarth</i>


01:20:36.897 --> 01:20:40.098
<i>and the key to the lockup where
Losberne kept the stolen paintings.</i>


01:20:50.433 --> 01:20:54.082
- Holy shit.
- <i>Even Bedwin and Brownlow deserved a break.</i>


01:20:54.112 --> 01:20:56.226
<i>In other arts-related news,</i>


01:20:56.257 --> 01:20:59.745
<i>a mystery painting arrived
with a special delivery</i>


01:20:59.776 --> 01:21:02.913
<i>for a new exhibition at
the National Gallery last week.</i>


01:21:02.945 --> 01:21:06.626
<i>The question everyone's asking
is: How did it get there?</i>


01:21:07.266 --> 01:21:10.369
<i>The painting was added
to the exhibition by mistake</i>


01:21:10.402 --> 01:21:13.538
<i>but critics have gone wild
for this unknown artist</i>


01:21:13.569 --> 01:21:16.290
<i>and have demanded
the piece remains on display.</i>


01:21:21.474 --> 01:21:22.914
There you go, Mum.


01:21:26.817 --> 01:21:30.753
<i>In fact, people can't stop
talking about the mystery artist,</i>


01:21:30.786 --> 01:21:33.506
<i>with many asking
who is Molly Twist</i>


01:21:33.537 --> 01:21:36.578
<i>and when and where
will all of her work appear.</i>


01:21:36.608 --> 01:21:39.969
<i>Dealers are said to be willing
to offer up to 50,000</i>


01:21:40.000 --> 01:21:43.009
<i>to anyone with
an original Twist painting.</i>


01:22:00.512 --> 01:22:02.113
Cheers, Nancy.


01:22:04.129 --> 01:22:06.977
Call me that again, Oliver,
and I will twist something you don't like.


01:22:09.249 --> 01:22:11.298
All right, quit canoodling.


01:22:13.952 --> 01:22:17.058
So, are you gonna stick
with us, kid?


01:22:17.089 --> 01:22:18.882
Come on,
you know you wanna.


01:22:18.914 --> 01:22:21.314
Look, if I'm gonna be
staying around,


01:22:21.345 --> 01:22:23.361
we gotta cut out all
the nonsense and go straight.


01:22:23.392 --> 01:22:26.561
- Whoa, wait.
- He's joking, right? That must be a joke.


01:22:26.593 --> 01:22:30.050
What exactly do you expect
us lot to do for a job, eh?


01:22:30.753 --> 01:22:32.706
You ever thought about
selling paintings?


01:22:33.666 --> 01:22:36.066
A bag full of Molly Twist art
is worth a few quid.


01:22:37.601 --> 01:22:38.594
Hmm?


01:22:39.393 --> 01:22:42.689
<i>Like I said, no singing,
no dancing.</i>


01:22:42.722 --> 01:22:44.802
<i>But maybe I was wrong about
the happy ending.</i>


01:22:45.762 --> 01:22:48.514
<i>I know these people.
I belong with them.</i>


01:25:36.482 --> 01:25:39.107
